# Anti-slop (shop UI)

When editing shop/landing components:

1. Do not invent layout if the existing Leonida editorial structure already covers the section.
2. No 3 equal feature cards with icons as the page skeleton.
3. No eyebrow kickers above headings.
4. No gradient text as the primary brand treatment (logo asset carries that).
5. No decorative glass panels that aren’t needed for interaction.
6. Keep CTAs as solid mist rectangles or hairline outlines — not pink→orange glow pills.
7. Explain spacing/type choices in terms of contrast and hierarchy, not “modern” / “sleek”.
